---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Framework from '../components/Framework.astro';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Methodology"
  description="The PairPilotFX decision framework: Context, Strength, Structure, Liquidity, Confirmation, and Risk."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <section class="section intro">
    <div class="container intro-grid">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">PairPilot methodology</p>
        <h1>Better decisions begin before the entry.</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="lead">
        PairPilotFX is built around a simple idea: traders should narrow uncertainty in stages rather than
        jump directly from a chart to a trade. The framework is designed to make that process explicit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <Framework />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container principle-grid">
      <article class="card card-pad">
        <p class="eyebrow">Context before direction</p>
        <h2>Start with the environment.</h2>
        <p>Macro conditions, event risk, and broader market behavior define what deserves caution before a directional idea is considered.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card card-pad">
        <p class="eyebrow">Evidence before conviction</p>
        <h2>Separate a scenario from confirmation.</h2>
        <p>A market thesis can be reasonable and still not be ready. PairPilotFX keeps the missing condition visible rather than treating expectation as evidence.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="radar">
    <div class="container radar card">
      <div class="radar-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">PairPilot Radar</p>
        <h2>Filter first. Analyze deeper second.</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Radar is the developing decision-support layer behind PairPilotFX. Its purpose is to reduce the
          number of markets demanding attention by applying the same framework consistently.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="radar-flow" aria-label="Radar filtering flow">
        <div><span>01</span><strong>Market context</strong><em>Is the environment usable?</em></div>
        <div><span>02</span><strong>Relative strength</strong><em>Is there meaningful separation?</em></div>
        <div><span>03</span><strong>Structure</strong><em>Is the multi-timeframe picture coherent?</em></div>
        <div><span>04</span><strong>Decision area</strong><em>Is price where the scenario matters?</em></div>
        <div><span>05</span><strong>Execution condition</strong><em>What still needs to happen?</em></div>
      </div>
      <p class="radar-note">
        Radar is decision support, not an automated signal service. Public product access will be introduced separately from the private PairPilotFX operational backend.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container closing">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">PairPilotFX</p>
        <h2>Guiding Better Trading Decisions.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="muted">Follow the weekly research to see the framework applied to live market preparation and review.</p>
        <a
          class="button"
          href="/weekly/"
          data-analytics-event="weekly_brief_cta_click"
          data-analytics-placement="methodology_closing"
        >Get the Weekly FX Brief →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .intro { padding-top: 100px; }
  .intro-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr .9fr; gap: 70px; align-items: end;
  }
  .intro h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); }
  .principle-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2,1fr); gap: 22px; }
  .principle-grid article { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .principle-grid h2 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.7rem); }
  .principle-grid article > p:last-child { color: var(--muted); }
  .radar { padding: clamp(28px,5vw,60px); border-color: var(--border-strong); }
  .radar-copy { display: grid; gap: 18px; max-width: 850px; }
  .radar-flow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5,1fr); gap: 10px; margin: 40px 0 26px; }
  .radar-flow div {
    display: grid; gap: 9px; min-height: 150px; padding: 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 16px; background: rgba(3,12,22,.30);
  }
  .radar-flow span { color: var(--accent); font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 850; }
  .radar-flow strong { font-size: .9rem; }
  .radar-flow em { color: var(--muted); font-style: normal; font-size: .78rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .radar-note { color: #8199b1; font-size: .82rem; }
  .closing {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr .85fr; gap: 50px; align-items: center;
  }
  .closing .stack { justify-items: start; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .intro-grid, .closing { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 30px; }
    .principle-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .radar-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .radar-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
